{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01001",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 6.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Ah, you know, hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.77,
      "end_seconds": 13.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Okay, of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.43,
      "end_seconds": 22.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.63,
      "end_seconds": 28.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Right, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.05,
      "end_seconds": 35.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "honestly, it's a stiff neck, and my family pushed me to come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.46,
      "end_seconds": 40.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Right, how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.78,
      "end_seconds": 52.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.08,
      "text": "I've had it for about a week. I've also had a high fever, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.34,
      "end_seconds": 57.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Has there been hating the light too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.93,
      "end_seconds": 72.06,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since last weekend. As for hating the light, maybe a five out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.88,
      "end_seconds": 79.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "So, have you had a stiff neck before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.87,
      "end_seconds": 89.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "mm, I had a similar thing about six months ago it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.0,
      "end_seconds": 91.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 92.88,
      "end_seconds": 102.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "it's febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day, doctor. He is on fluoxetine, every morning, I give it to him"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.34,
      "end_seconds": 106.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 107.77,
      "end_seconds": 119.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "It's 20 milligrams. Hmm, he is on bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day for the heart rhythm, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.99,
      "end_seconds": 141.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Right, have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.93,
      "end_seconds": 147.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Yes, um, I had a varicose vein procedure, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.22,
      "end_seconds": 169.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.27,
      "end_seconds": 175.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Actually, yes, tramadol, it gives me vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.82,
      "end_seconds": 180.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Okay, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.06,
      "end_seconds": 194.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I retired from the post office two years ago. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.39,
      "end_seconds": 198.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.07,
      "end_seconds": 206.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Gout, for two years. Well, I have depression, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.95,
      "end_seconds": 209.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.06,
      "end_seconds": 215.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "An irregular heartbeat, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.11,
      "end_seconds": 225.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Okay, I can see gout and depression in your file as well. Any recent head injury or cough at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.38,
      "end_seconds": 230.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "erm, no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.45,
      "end_seconds": 236.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.64,
      "end_seconds": 240.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.37,
      "end_seconds": 259.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.1,
      "end_seconds": 269.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.49,
      "end_seconds": 292.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "okay: oxygen saturation is 95 percent, BP is 120 over 66, pulse is 90 beats a minute, temperature is 38.7 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.24,
      "end_seconds": 295.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.61,
      "end_seconds": 300.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.38,
      "end_seconds": 305.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.7,
      "end_seconds": 309.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.0,
      "end_seconds": 334.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Your neck is stiff, you are feverish, and there are purple spots that do not fade when pressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.39,
      "end_seconds": 372.69,
      "duration_seconds": 34.3,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Putting it all together, it's hard to say. Possible bacterial meningitis is one possibility and meningococcal septicaemia another, and I'd rather not commit yet. We should do a lumbar puncture for possible meningitis. We should do blood cultures for possible meningitis. I'd like you to take benzylpenicillin, 1.2 grams, once now, single dose. That should help with possible meningitis. Call an ambulance now, this is an emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.67,
      "end_seconds": 391.28,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. One warning sign to remember: you cannot go now. In that case don't wait. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.13,
      "end_seconds": 394.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}